"After 1 year, $(C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (5, 0, 9, 3)$."
This matches. Alien 1 receives 0.
"After 2 years, $(C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (4, 1, 9, 3)$."
At year 2, Alien 2 becomes adult.
Adults present: Alien 1.
Alien 1 has 5 stones ($\ge 1$). So Alien 1 gives 1 stone to Alien 2.
Alien 1's stones decrease by 1: $5 \to 4$.
Alien 2's stones increase by 1: $0 \to 1$.
Result: $[4, 1, 9, 3]$. Matches.
"After 3 years, $(C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (3, 0, 11, 3)$."
At year 3, Alien 3 becomes adult.
Adults present: Alien 1, Alien 2.
Alien 1 has 4 stones ($\ge 1$). Gives 1.
Alien 2 has 1 stone ($\ge 1$). Gives 1.
Total received by Alien 3: 2.
Alien 1: $4 \to 3$.
Alien 2: $1 \to 0$.
Alien 3: $9 \to 9 + 2 = 11$.
Result: $[3, 0, 11, 3]$. Matches.
"After 4 years, $(C_1, C_2, C_3, C_4) = (2, 0, 10, 5)$."
At year 4, Alien 4 becomes adult.
