If we have a set of potential top mochi $S_{top}$ and a set of potential bottom mochi $S_{bot}$, we want to match them.
Since $A$ is sorted, if we pick a subset of indices $I$ to be the top mochi and a subset $J$ to be the bottom mochi, with $|I| = |J| = K$, and $I \cap J = \emptyset$, we want to check if there exists a bijection $f: I \to J$ such that $A_i \le A_{f(i)}/2$ for all $i \in I$.
Since $A$ is sorted, if we sort $I$ and $J$ (which are already sorted indices), say $i_1 < i_2 < \dots < i_K$ and $j_1 < j_2 < \dots < j_K$, does it make sense to pair $i_k$ with $j_k$?
